Recommends: ca-certificates
Description: Run Android apps as native Linux processes
 Mosaic runs an Android app as an ordinary host process instead of booting a
 whole Android system in a container. An installed app is a desktop
 application: it opens a real Wayland window and its data lives under its own
 system user. AOSP's ART and Bionic are reused as host-native libraries, and
 the Android API surface, framework services, Binder and the hardware
 abstraction layer are translated to host equivalents.
